. The company was founded in 2007 and is headquartered in Arlington, Virginia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Parth  Mehrotra | CEO & Director | Age 46 | Compensation: $1.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $1.7M ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 22%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $58K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Privia Health Group, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $3.1B market cap on $2.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +16% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 6.2% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 168% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.675234097513723},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $15.7M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-15665443.91},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead 